{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3276","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3276\",\"parent_revision\":\"d32589732e63f299f758a231d0baebffb081eab2\",\"root_revision\":\"1fc9dfbc859dab7833fe8c674a1a802f9858a8798761f85444deff93d1daa965\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`agents/contract-verification.md` line 151 states: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\" This assumes a synchronous dispatch model where the caller receives the subagent's final text as a direct return value.\\n\\nObserved during this session while running `/dh:implement-feature` on plan Pd95e593c for #3151: dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the `Agent` tool returned only an async \\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment. The agent completed its analysis and went idle twice (confirmed via `ListAgents`), but no message with actual content was ever delivered back \u2014 only bare `idle_notification` events with no `summary` field, unlike every other subagent dispatched in the same session (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer, feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0/t1 task agents), all of which reported back with a `summary` field containing real content. Sending the idle agent a direct follow-up question asking it to restate its verdict also produced no reply.\\n\\nThe `Agent` tool's own documentation states: \\\"Your plain text output is NOT visible to other agents \u2014 to communicate, you MUST call [SendMessage].\\\" That is the observed cause: `contract-verification.md`'s instructions never tell the agent to call `SendMessage`; they tell it to just \\\"output\\\" its finding as its response, consistent with a synchronous dispatch model this environment does not use for agent-tool dispatch.\\n\\nImpact: `implement-feature`'s Progress Loop step 4a (post-task contract verification) silently produces no usable result under this environment's async dispatch \u2014 the orchestrator either blocks indefinitely waiting for a message that never arrives, or gives up and has to verify the contract manually (as happened this session), defeating the point of delegating the check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: this is the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent \u2014 `git log` shows a merged commit \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" that added exactly this kind of completion-report step to `dh:impact-analyst`. `dh:contract-verification` appears to have been missed by that same fix, and other `dh:*` agents dispatched by the same Progress Loop may share the identical gap \u2014 not verified for any agent besides contract-verification in this session.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) add an explicit `SendMessage` step to `contract-verification.md`'s Output Format section, mirroring whatever change PR #3249 made to `impact-analyst.md`; (2) audit the other `dh:*` agents invoked by `implement-feature`/`add-new-feature`'s Progress Loop for the same synchronous-response assumption, since any could have the identical gap and it would surface the same way (silent, not an error).\\n\\n**User-provided context** (added during grooming, 2026-08-29): another possible direction for grooming/planning to evaluate, not a requirement \u2014 don't make `dh:contract-verification` (or any sibling agent with the same gap) into a `TeamCreate` teammate just to get a working report-back channel. Keep it a plain background `Agent()` spawn, but have it write its result directly to the backend (e.g. `backlog_groom` on the Concerns section, or `artifact_register`, mirroring how `dh:t0-baseline-capture` reports) instead of relying on a returned value or on `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\")` \u2014 there is no team-lead when there is no team.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:41:39.625254Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: contract-verification agent's findings never reach the orchestrator under async subagent dispatch\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Determine why contract-verification's findings never reach the implement-feature orchestrator under async Agent() dispatch, and specify the correct fix consistent with current architecture direction.\\nConditions:\\n1. Agent() tool dispatch is asynchronous for non-fork subagents in this environment (no synchronous return of final text to the caller) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. contract-verification is dispatched via a bare `Agent()` call in implement-feature/SKILL.md step 4a, not via TeamCreate teammate pattern | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. contract-verification.md's current \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there\\\" line was a deliberate change in PR #3202 (`route agent handoffs through the backend, not SendMessage`), which replaced an earlier SendMessage-to-team-lead pattern \u2014 it is not an oversight from PR #3249's impact-analyst-specific fix | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Whether other dh:* agents dispatched via bare Agent() in implement-feature/add-new-feature's Progress Loop share the identical synchronous-return assumption | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Established backend-routing pattern for single-shot (non-team) verification agents \u2014 e.g. dh:t0-baseline-capture registers results via `artifact_register` instead of relying on a returned value \u2014 that contract-verification could adopt | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Whether SendMessage from a standalone (non-team) Agent()-spawned agent reaches the orchestrator's context in this environment at all, or only teammates spawned via TeamCreate can address a \\\"team-lead\\\" | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:50:36.568308Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n\\n**Rationale**: The same root cause (async dispatch + no SendMessage / backend completion) has appeared in at least 2 confirmed backlog items (#3248, #3276) plus 4+ additional agents identified in audit #3250. This is not an isolated defect but a systematic assumption baked into multiple agent files before the async dispatch architecture was widely understood. The pattern repeats because there was no enforcement gate when PR #3249 fixed impact-analyst \u2014 it was fixed in isolation without auditing sibling agents or documenting the required pattern.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: 6-sigma frequency analysis via backlog history search\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agent spawned via `Agent()` tool completes analysis but findings silently vanish because instructions assume synchronous return and never call SendMessage \u2192 Agent explicitly reports findings back to orchestrator via SendMessage (for async dispatch) or backend method (for non-team spawn).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:50:28.405304Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: 3 additional affected systems beyond the two originally cited (contract-verification.md, implement-feature/SKILL.md): dispatch-contract/SKILL.md (root doctrine authorizing the broken pattern), subagent-contract/SKILL.md (the general contract contract-verification overrides), and groom/error.md (a second, independent bare-Agent() dispatch with the identical bug, in a different workflow).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \u2014 the broken agent. Line 151: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\" A load-bearing false assumption under bare `Agent()` dispatch. Its `tools:` frontmatter (line 5) still grants `SendMessage` \u2014 the grant was never revoked, only the instruction to use it was removed by commit 11082f0eb. Needs an explicit reporting mechanism restored.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (step 4a, lines 151-207) \u2014 spawns `Agent(subagent_type=\\\"dh:contract-verification\\\", ...)` as a bare, non-TeamCreate, non-task-worker call (line 163), then line 187 treats the result as synchronous (\\\"If the contract-verification agent returns a `<concerns>` block...\\\"). Under this runtime's async non-fork `Agent()` dispatch, that check always sees nothing \u2014 contract concerns are silently dropped every time, with no error signal. This is the direct symptom the item describes.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md` (Agent Failure procedure, lines 15-33) \u2014 a second, independent bare `Agent(subagent_type=\\\"dh:task-worker\\\", ...)` dispatch (line 18) whose result (`last_success`, `first_failure`, `failure_type`) is branched on synchronously by a mermaid decision tree in Step 4. Same defect class, different workflow. Under async dispatch this diagnostic branch is unreachable \u2014 the \\\"2nd failure -> Escalation\\\" workflow-block logic is currently dead code.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\nNone identified beyond the producer/consumer/agent-instruction entries above.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\nNone identified \u2014 no user-facing docs describe this dispatch contract; the affected instructions are agent/skill files, covered under Agent Instructions below.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` \u2014 `<dispatch_selection>` states: \\\"A dispatch that hands over no dh operation \u2014 an independent review whose finding is its response \u2014 has nothing here to reach: any specialist that fits runs it, dh roster or not.\\\" This doctrine legitimizes the exact broken pattern \u2014 it documents \\\"finding is my response\\\" as a valid dispatch category, when under this runtime's actual async non-fork `Agent()` semantics it never is. Until this changes, contract-verification is the reference implementation of a codified anti-pattern that future agent authors will reproduce.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` \u2014 `<result_destination>` (correct in itself): \\\"Put your result where your own agent file says... Where neither names one: deliverables go in repository files; every other document is an artifact, registered with `artifact_register`... Hand the next step a plan, task, or artifact id.\\\" This is the fallback contract-verification's own file opts out of via an explicit override. The fix likely means either removing contract-verification's override (fall back to this artifact-based contract) or adding an equally explicit, dispatch-context-correct override.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n1. `contract-verification.md` \u2014 producer, HIGH risk, broken today (silent no-op)\\n2. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u00a74a \u2014 consumer, HIGH risk, broken today\\n3. `dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` \u2014 agent-instruction / root doctrine, HIGH risk (actively misleading once contract-verification is fixed unless updated in the same change)\\n4. `subagent-contract/SKILL.md` \u2014 agent-instruction, LOW-MEDIUM risk (override clause is technically correct, just exploited by contract-verification's opt-out)\\n5. `impact-analyst.md` \u2014 sibling agent, comparison baseline only, not itself broken. Fixed in PR #3249 (commit 43058f345) via `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\", ...)` \u2014 but impact-analyst is dispatched via `TeamCreate`, where \\\"team-lead\\\" is a real addressable teammate. contract-verification is dispatched via bare `Agent()` from inside a skill run with no team-lead teammate to address, so a verbatim copy of this fix would not resolve correctly.\\n6. `t0-baseline-capture.md` / `tn-verification-gate.md` \u2014 precedent, not broken. Register results via `artifact_register` (types `T0-baseline`, `TN-verification`); the consuming step reads them back via `artifact_read` rather than depending on the dispatch call's return value. Strongest available precedent for the fix.\\n7. `groom/error.md` \\\"Agent Failure\\\" procedure \u2014 consumer, MEDIUM-HIGH risk, same defect class, different workflow (see Consumers above).\\n8. `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 verified clean. Zero bare `Agent(` calls (grep confirmed). Its Progress Loop dispatches via delegation prompts that instruct the agent to call `artifact_register` itself and return a `STATUS: DONE / path:` marker; the orchestrator then verifies via `artifact list --item-id {issue} --artifact-type {type}` and explicitly must NOT call `artifact_register` itself as a workaround. Correct pattern, should not be touched by this fix.\\n\\nNo test file references `contract-verification`, its `<concerns>` output contract, or the groom `error.md` diagnostic dispatch \u2014 verification risk is HIGH for both consumer sites: this defect has no automated guard and surfaces only as \\\"contract concerns never appear in backlog items,\\\" a silent absence that's easy to miss.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible \u2014 contract-verification.md needs an explicit reporting mechanism restored\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface \u2014 implement-feature/SKILL.md \u00a74a and groom/error.md's Agent Failure procedure both need to read the result from wherever it now lands\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 N/A, no user-facing docs affected\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated \u2014 dispatch-contract/SKILL.md's \\\"finding is my response\\\" category needs qualifying or removing (or scoping explicitly to dispatch contexts where a synchronous/addressable return actually holds)\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing) \u2014 N/A\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated \u2014 N/A, none identified\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-28/29, while running /dh:implement-feature on plan Pd95e593c (#3151), dispatching dh:contract-verification for task T1\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:50:36.568270Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 6-sigma frequency analysis via backlog history search\\n\\n**Frequency**: 2+ confirmed occurrences, plus 4+ additional instances identified in audit #3250\\n\\n**Matches**:\\n- #3248 \u2014 \\\"fix: impact-analyst agent never sends a completion message back to the orchestrator\\\" \u2014 2026-08 (open)\\n- #3276 \u2014 \\\"fix: contract-verification agent's findings never reach the orchestrator under async subagent dispatch\\\" \u2014 2026-08 (open, current)\\n\\n**Pattern**: Multiple `dh:*` agents were written with the assumption that their final text output would be returned synchronously to the caller, but the `Agent()` tool provides async dispatch where final text is invisible \u2014 agents must call `SendMessage` to reach the orchestrator. This assumption persists across at least 6 agents in the codebase (impact-analyst, contract-verification, rtica-assessor, classifier, backlog-item-groomer, alignment-analyst).\\n\\n**Improvement**: Establish a documentation-and-review gate requiring all `dh:*` agents dispatched via `Agent()` tool to include an explicit completion-report step in their output format (calling `SendMessage(to=\\\"main\\\", message=...)` or writing findings via backend method like `artifact_register` / `backlog_groom`), and audit all existing agents against this requirement in a follow-up chore.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c82efb78e68edcc4cb0f44796085c3b5fc6a463020ec413704476eff7029df23\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRYZJg\"}"}